# Simple experimental RMK config for Saurus keyboard.

With Nix:
  nix develop
  cargo make uf2 --release

Install tools:
  cargo install cargo-make flip-link

Then build with this command:
  cargo make uf2 --release

The cargo-make firmware tasks run `cargo update -p rmk` first, so they build the
latest commit from RMK's `main` branch. A plain `cargo build` still honors the
revision in Cargo.lock; run `cargo update -p rmk` first when building directly.
